 "caption": "Gifford et al. 2014 Lab Chip 14, 4496\u20134505, Fig. 4 inset (the 300 \u00b5m bar, 107.52 px; the legs at 45.78\u00b0 on the image, from the post columns) with the rejected variant gifford2014_fig4_pathorder (rc7's reading B, legs in path order): leg 4's last post rows and the leads beyond (cyan: the reproduction claim), and the neighbouring leg (leg 3) at the preset's leg spacing, read on this inset (amber: its centre line and post pitch are the image's; its side-channel walls are compared with the image's below; the claim statistic is leg 4's outline only).  Registration: scale from the bar, rotation measured on the image; translation fitted on features and, independently, by chamfer matching (they agree within 0.1 / 0.0 px along / across).  Nearest-outline offset: median 0.62 \u00b5m, 90th percentile 1.40 \u00b5m (n 7277); for comparison 3.97 \u00b5m with the mask shifted half a pitch along and 3.88 \u00b5m with it shifted 5 \u00b5m across.  Over every eligible sample: the metric found an outline for 99.9 % of the 7281 eligible samples (coverage 0.999); censored null ratios 8.54 (half a pitch) and 6.37 (5 \u00b5m across); chamfer null ratios 2.89 and 2.38.  On the image: leg 4's post columns 159.2 \u00b5m apart (mask w_c + l_g = 159.5), pitch 45.83 / 45.84 \u00b5m (mask 45.8); the legs' centrelines 818 \u00b5m apart (mask 818).  The neighbouring leg's side-channel walls read -0.8 to +1.0 \u00b5m against the mask's (+ = the image's channel wider; 3 wall classes of at least 50 samples, measured.leg2_side_walls): their mean offsets within 3 \u00b5m (a mean over the window, blind to a slope: the taper direction is V13's, taper_sign.py).",
